minios-tools (1.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bind converter inputs to retained descriptors so path replacement cannot
    redirect compression, extraction, or source hashing.
  * Stage conversions in identity-checked private directories and roll back
    only outputs whose published inode is still owned.
  * Use the renameat2 syscall on Bionic glibc and fail closed when atomic
    no-replace directory publication is unavailable.
  * Reject every non-zero unsquashfs result instead of publishing a partial
    extraction, including failed pre-extraction listings.
  * Reap complete converter process groups, validate staged modules with
    unsquashfs, and emit pure NDJSON under --json.
  * Make legacy build wrappers propagate failed inner operations, copy dotfiles,
    and parse apt target releases without treating values as packages.
  * Add pure-NDJSON `apt2sb --json`, keep APT diagnostics off machine stdout,
    wrap the final savechanges result, and bind local package reads to the
    invoking `pkexec` user.
  * Add pure-NDJSON `script2sb --json`, bind script and machine-mode seed
    inputs to the invoking `pkexec` user, and use no-follow filesystem-engine
    copying without changing legacy `cp -a` behavior.
  * Add split `chroot2sb prepare/shell/finish/cancel` lifecycle for embedded
    terminals, with root-owned opaque sessions, caller binding, flock
    serialization, and device/inode-verified private workspaces.
  * Resolve AUFS writable and lower branches through the mounted session's
    ordered sysfs records when mountinfo reports only the session identifier.
  * Bind legacy wrapper captures to their temporary mounted unions and select
    the effective Dracut OverlayFS upper directory by default.
  * Preserve exact capture of OverlayFS whiteouts whose extra hard link belongs
    only to the external workdir, while still rejecting in-tree non-regular
    hard-link topology.
  * Refresh command manuals and keep the engine responsibility notes concise.
  * Make `sb list` rootless, add stable `sb list --json` runtime module output,
    and gate runtime mutations on the filesystem actually mounted at `/`.
  * Add rootless `sb next-boot [--json]` using the effective MiniOS data tree,
    current boot filters, source override precedence, and Debian live-layout
    compatibility without adding a new initramfs state contract.
  * Add rootless `sb inspect FILE [--json]` for fail-closed SquashFS content
    inspection without extracting the module.
  * Move `sb` machine-protocol serialization into `minios_protocol.py` and
    reuse the existing filesystem engine for no-follow module-store mutations,
    eliminating inline Python from Bash frontends.
  * Add privileged `sb next-boot add/remove` with durable-store selection,
    caller-bound source access, no-follow dirfd mutations, staged SquashFS
    validation, atomic no-replace publication, and read-only base protection.
  * Resolve Python helpers relative to the installed `usr/bin` layout as well
    as the source tree and canonical `/usr/lib/minios-tools` location.
  * Make rootless `sb2dir` restore only user xattrs so root-only OverlayFS
    metadata does not reject otherwise extractable MiniOS modules.
  * Remove the repository-local translation update script; translation refreshes
    are driven by lokit from the main MiniOS repository.
  * Fix the remaining AUFS session-id transformation flagged by ShellCheck.
  * Add the SquashFS running-session save backend and shutdown helper used by
    MiniOS core, so shutdown saves do not depend on Session Manager.
  * Build base-module fingerprints only from the mounted union lower layers;
    numbered persistence snapshots no longer masquerade as duplicate modules.
  * Preserve shared OverlayFS 0:0 whiteouts semantically during exact capture,
    including the hard-linked whiteouts created by package removal.
  * Surface the common SquashFS save backend error when shutdown saving fails.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 21:30:00 +0300

minios-tools (1.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remove the sb2iso executable, completion, documentation, and manual page;
    ISO mastering is owned by the new minios-image-builder-cli package.
  * Add exact, narrow clean, and selected savechanges profiles plus private
    schema-2 JSON inventory, strict selection, union metadata, and xattr rules
  * Run savechanges through an isolated Python engine with retained dirfds and
    replay-safe OverlayFS xattr and selected-opacity policy
  * Bind captures to boot and base-module fingerprints and honour caller-owned
    cancel markers so an unprivileged caller can cooperatively stop and reap
    the complete privileged savechanges process tree
  * Use mounted-root union detection and non-installable non-root
    source-test overrides
  * Resolve mkfs.ext2 from the trusted system path and depend on e2fsprogs
  * Rewrite dir2sb and sb2dir as rootless, non-destructive converters with
    private staging, bounded cancellation, exact argv handling, and atomic
    no-replace publication.
  * Emit stable phase events and a machine-readable result under --json.
  * Move the savechanges transaction into its separately installed Python
    engine with an isolated interpreter and sanitized environment.
  * Retire destructive rmsbdir, sb rm, and sb rmdir behavior; compatibility
    commands now refuse unmount and recursive deletion.
  * Make exact session capture fail closed on unsupported objects, unreadable
    or non-preservable xattrs, malformed AUFS whiteouts, and unsafe topology.
  * Bind OverlayFS and AUFS capture to the mounted writable layer and bind base
    attestation to ordered mounted block-device bytes.
  * Publish a versioned extraction footprint and account for simultaneous
    staging, compression, and no-replace publication resources.
  * Support the Bats 0.4 temporary-directory environment shipped by Bionic.
  * Declare Python, SquashFS, and xattr tools used by the package test suite.
  * Require the MiniOS Bionic SquashFS backport that provides zstd modules.
  * Keep real-tool tests compatible with Bionic attr and Python 3.6.
  * Bump script versions: dir2sb 2.0.0, sb2dir 2.0.0, savechanges 1.3.0.

 -- crims0n <crims0n@minios.dev>  Mon, 10 Aug 2026 00:29:10 +0300

